From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 05:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: clear EXL for ERL userspace return

The physical SF2000 now reaches the final restore path with ErrorEPC set to
the /init entry point, but the saved status is 0x8017: both ERL and EXL are
set. On MIPS, eret in ERL mode returns via ErrorEPC and clears ERL. It does
not take the normal EXL return path, leaving EXL set and preventing the CPU
from entering normal user execution.

For the SF2000 identity-userspace path, clear EXL when preparing the initial
userspace status. Also clear and log it in the final restore hook as a guard
against any later path reintroducing EXL before eret.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/process.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
@@ -84,6 +84,11 @@ void sf2000_ret_before_restore(struct pt_regs *regs)
 	sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-epc", 9, regs->cp0_epc);
 	if (!(regs->cp0_status & ST0_ERL))
 		return;
+	if (regs->cp0_status & ST0_EXL) {
+		regs->cp0_status &= ~ST0_EXL;
+		sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-status-fixed", 9,
+			regs->cp0_status);
+	}
 
 	sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-errorepc-before", 9,
 		read_c0_errorepc());
@@ -112,6 +117,7 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs * regs, unsigned long pc, unsigned long sp)
 	status |= KU_USER;
 	if (sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled()) {
 		status |= ST0_ERL;
+		status &= ~ST0_EXL;
 		sp = SF2000_IDENTITY_USER_STACK;
 		sf2000_progress_mark("mips-start-thread-ebase", 9,
 			read_c0_ebase());
-- 
